3. definitions.md: 'Each dropping set is a union of arithmetic progressions (a fact...)'
==============================================================================
  Terras: sigma(n) = stopping time (shortcut map T), omega(n) = coefficient stopping time
  = first j with 3^(odd steps) < 2^j.  'Dset_k is exactly a union of residue classes'
  holds iff sigma(n) = omega(n) for all n >= 2 (Coefficient Stopping Time conjecture).
  n = 1: (sigma, omega) = (None, 2)  -> 1 lies in the class 1 mod 4 (omega = 2) but never drops: the reason for 'n > 1'
  2 <= n <= 2000000: violations of sigma = omega: 0 []
  Dset_k for 2 <= n < 2^18, k <= 16:  E = k - s, residues mod 2^E, exact union of classes?
    k= 1  oddities=[0]  E= 1  #classes=  1  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k= 3  oddities=[1]  E= 2  #classes=  1  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k= 6  oddities=[2]  E= 4  #classes=  1  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k= 8  oddities=[3]  E= 5  #classes=  2  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k=11  oddities=[4]  E= 7  #classes=  3  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k=13  oddities=[5]  E= 8  #classes=  7  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
    k=16  oddities=[6]  E=10  #classes= 12  Dset_k == union of those classes (n>1): True
  counts of classes above are A100982 with the class 'even' in front: 1,1,2,3,7,12
  checked n <= 2000000 [this script]: exact for every s <= 4960, i.e. Dset_k for k <= 12822
  checked n <= 10000000 [site_audit/explore_check_sturmian (F)]: exact for every s <= 10945, i.e. Dset_k for k <= 28293
  checked n <= 2.8E+19 [Rozier-Terracol 2026, Cor. 5.4]: exact for every s <= 200000, i.e. Dset_k for k <= 516993 (at least; search capped)
  Any nontrivial positive cycle would be a violator (its least element has omega finite,
  sigma infinite), as n = 1 is: 'class = dropping set for every k' implies no nontrivial
  cycle, so it cannot be 'a fact that follows from the affine orbit structure'.
  Lagarias 1985 sec. 2: Coefficient Stopping Time Conjecture (Terras), open.

