8. publications.md: what the two 'connections' of Paper 1 are
==============================================================================
  Orbital triple (collatz/geometry.py): (n^2 - d^2, 2nd, n^2 + d^2) = Euclid's formula on (n, d).
  identity holds for 1000 random integer pairs with no relation to Collatz: True
  'Riemann' link (paper sec. 5.2): z = n + n i, z' = (n - d) + d i, z0 = z'/z, 'Re z0 = 1/2'.
  Re(z'/z) over 1000 random real pairs (n, d): min 0.500000000000 max 0.500000000000
  -> ((n-d) + d i)/(n(1+i)) = 1/2 + i(2d-n)/(2n) identically: true for any two numbers.
